{% doc %}
  The two timestamps a status change decides: when the ticket was closed,
  and when it was marked solved.

  Both are set when the ticket enters a status of that category and blank
  otherwise, so moving back out clears them. A ticket that went solved,
  then open, then solved again should say when it was solved this time,
  not the first time.

  Four endpoints change a status. Working this out in each of them is four
  chances to get it wrong in three of them.

  @param {object} status - The status the ticket is moving to
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign now = 'now' | date: '%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'

  assign closed_at = null
  assign solved_at = null

  if status.kind == 'closed'
    assign closed_at = now
    comment
      A closed ticket is a solved one that stopped waiting, so solved_at
      stays set. "When did we consider this answered" then has one answer
      whether the ticket is sitting in Confirmation or has since closed.
    endcomment
    assign solved_at = now
  elsif status.kind == 'solved'
    assign solved_at = now
  endif

  assign stamps = { "closed_at": closed_at, "solved_at": solved_at }
  return stamps
%}
